# Custos Air-Gapped Install — __VERSION__

This bundle (`custos-__VERSION__-airgapped.tar.gz`) is self-contained: it ships
the Custos Helm chart with every dependency subchart vendored, a `docker save`
archive of every required container image, the `connectors-core` OCI artifact,
and SHA-256 checksums. No internet access is required on the target cluster.

## Contents

```
chart/custos/         Helm chart with vendored dependency subcharts
images/*.tar          docker save archive per image (see images.txt)
connectors/           connectors-core OCI artifact (or a mirror note)
checksums.sha256      SHA-256 of every bundled file
INSTALL-AIRGAPPED.md  this runbook
```

## Prerequisites on the target side

- A host with `kubectl`, `helm`, and `skopeo` (or `docker`) that can reach both
  the cluster API and your internal OCI registry (`registry.internal/custos`).
- The CloudNativePG and External Secrets operators installed cluster-wide
  (their images are listed under "cluster prerequisites" in `images.txt`).

## Steps

1. **Verify checksums**

   ```bash
   tar -xzf custos-__VERSION__-airgapped.tar.gz
   cd custos-__VERSION__-airgapped
   sha256sum -c checksums.sha256   # or: shasum -a 256 -c checksums.sha256
   ```

2. **Load and mirror the images into your internal registry**

   The air-gapped values files are pre-wired to pull from a mirror registry
   (`registry.internal`, with the Custos + Bitnami images under
   `registry.internal/custos` and Dapr / cert-manager / Prometheus directly
   under `registry.internal`). Edit `global.imageRegistry` (and the per-subchart
   registry overrides alongside it) in
   `chart/custos/values-airgapped-<profile>.yaml` to match your registry before
   installing.

   The chart rewrites image paths per subchart, so there is no single string
   rule that maps every source image to its mirror target. Instead, render the
   chosen profile to get the authoritative source-to-target mapping and push
   each loaded archive to the reference the install actually expects:

   ```bash
   # 1. Load every archived image locally.
   for tar in images/*.tar; do docker load -q -i "$tar"; done

   # 2. For each image the air-gapped profile renders, retag the matching loaded
   #    image (matched by repository name + tag) and push it to your mirror.
   helm template custos chart/custos -f chart/custos/values-airgapped-ha.yaml \
       --set oidc.keycloak.enabled=true --set secrets.sealed.enabled=true \
     | grep -hoE 'image: "?[^"]+' | sed -E 's/image: "?//' | sort -u \
     | while read -r target; do
         tag="${target##*:}"; name="${target%:*}"; name="${name##*/}"
         src="$(docker images --format '{{.Repository}}:{{.Tag}}' \
                  | grep -E "(^|/)${name}:${tag}\$" | head -n1)"
         [ -z "$src" ] && { echo "no archive for $target" >&2; continue; }
         docker tag "$src" "$target"
         docker push "$target"
       done
   ```

   (`skopeo copy docker-archive:images/<file>.tar docker://<target>` works
   equivalently and needs no local Docker daemon.)

3. **Push the `connectors-core` OCI artifact** into the same registry (see
   `connectors/`).

4. **Configure Layer-2 secrets** — install Vault, or apply Sealed Secrets, and
   populate the connection/credential secrets the chart expects.

5. **Configure the OIDC issuer** — install Keycloak (bundled) or point the chart
   at an existing issuer; wire identity federation if desired.

6. **Install Custos**

   ```bash
   helm install custos chart/custos \
     -f chart/custos/values-airgapped-ha.yaml \
     --set global.imageRegistry=registry.internal/custos
   ```

7. **Verify**

   ```bash
   kubectl -n custos-system get pods
   ```

See `design/architecture/reference-deployment.md` for the full air-gapped
reference recipe.
